From 5ad9d5fccfec7f1df25b654e0f1b2dcdcc67f644 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:20:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] lifecycle guard: printf `*` width/precision, `%.Ns`
 truncation, `%b` escapes and `-v NAME` no longer hide the printed command
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The output-sink walk read `printf FMT ARGS` output as "each conversion takes the next
argument whole". Four bash printf behaviours broke that, so a shell sink ran a command the
guard never saw (allowed while bash ran an oversized, unscannable script):

- `printf '%*s %s' 5 bash /x/huge.sh | bash`: `*` takes an argument as the width.
- `printf '%.4s %s' bashrc /x/huge.sh | bash`: precision truncates `bashrc` to `bash`.
- `printf '%b %s' 'ba\x73h' /x/huge.sh | bash`: `%b` decodes `\xHH`/`\0NNN`, ends at `\c`.
- `printf -v x '%s %s' bash /x/huge.sh; echo $x | bash`: `-v` takes NAME as its operand, so
  the walk read `x` as the format (review of PR #2341 @d532aef7d4, t_01a1d6051a931de9).

cron/lifecycle_guard_printf.py (added by #2341 with a whole-argument `_printf_output`) now
models bash 5's printf builtin: flags, width and precision as digits or `*` (negative widths
left-justify, negative precision is none), length modifiers, csbqQdiouxXeEfFgGaA and %(FMT)T
conversions, strtoimax argument parsing ('c, 0x, 0NNN, prefixes), format-string escapes,
`%b`/`echo -e` escapes with `\c`, format reuse, and an invalid conversion ending the output.
Widths and numeric precision are capped at 4096. A parametrized test checks the model byte
for byte against real bash. The format is found past `-v NAME`, `-vNAME` and `--`.

Printed text is now also walked with escapes decoded printf-style and echo-style, so
`printf 'ba\x73h %s'`, `echo -e 'ba\x73h …'` and `print('ba\x73h …')` are caught too.

The wrong "imprecision can only add a line to scan" docstring and the "width and precision
are dropped (only adds text)" test comment are gone.

FILE_LINES: printed_argument_lines/with_escapes_decoded (and their two regexes) move into
the printf module, so cron/lifecycle_guard.py ends at 1947 lines (main: 1974).

Proof (bash 5.2.21):
- Real bash runs the named script for every new shape (marker scripts print RAN-…).
- The new tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_output_sink.py against main 82cbdd4b51: 10 sink
  shapes fail (printf-star-width, printf-star-precision, printf-precision, printf-b-hex,
  printf-b-octal, printf-b-stop, printf-v, echo-e-hex, echo-e-octal, print-hex);
  this tree: 165 passed.
- heredoc_shape_corpus.py report --full: cases=22212 refused=18904 violations=0.
- Mutants: 33/33 of the printf model and its wiring (before the rebase onto #2341) and 4/4
  of the `-v` format index killed.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: ok.
